      "message": "Can we instead expose a `get_target_config(...)` function (similar to `get_target_outputs(...)`) which returns the resolved config for the target during execution?\n\nThen you can do:\n\n```\nsource_set(\"foo\") {\n  ...\n}\n\nwrite_file(\n  \"$root_out_dir/foo_config.json\",\n  get_target_config(\":foo\"),\n  \"json\")\n```\n\nThis would have the same limitation as `get_target_outputs(...)` in that it can only be used in a target defined in the same file, before the call to the function (but it does not looks like this would be a problem for your use case).\n\nThis remove the need to write additional code to write files, add them to the list of known generated files, support hard dependencies, .... which `write_file(...)` already handle.\n\nDrawback is that people may start to use `get_target_config(...)` for other uses.",
